<title>USA: OUTLOOK -- U.S Brokers' Q3 seen hit by summer tumult.</title>
<headline>OUTLOOK -- U.S Brokers' Q3 seen hit by summer tumult.</headline>
<byline>Richard Melville</byline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The stock market's see-saw summer, which sidelined jittery investors and wreaked havoc with initial public offering calendars, also robbed brokerages of any hope to match powerful second quarter results.</p>
<p>&quot;The trend would appear to be that profits in the third quarter will be lower than those in the second,&quot; said Perrin Long, an independent analyst. &quot;I think it will be the case across the board.&quot;</p>
</text>
